---
import LegalLayout from '@layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE, mailHref } from '@data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="The terms and conditions that apply when you enrol in a course, use our website, or interact with PTCA admissions and training services in Karachi."
  updated="10 April 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to your use of this website and to enrolments in any
    programme offered by {SITE.legalName}.
  </p>

  <h2>Course information</h2>
  <p>
    Course content, duration, schedule and learning mode are confirmed at the time
    of registration. Fees and batch dates may change between intakes, so please
    rely on the confirmation you receive from admissions rather than information
    shown on a general webpage.
  </p>

  <h2>Registration and payment</h2>
  <p>
    A place in a batch is confirmed once registration and the applicable fee have
    been completed as advised by admissions. Course fees are not refundable except
    where stated in our refund policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Attendance and conduct</h2>
  <p>
    Learners are expected to attend their sessions regularly and to conduct
    themselves professionally. Repeated absence without notice may affect your
    eligibility to sit an assessment or receive a certificate.
  </p>

  <h2>Certificates</h2>
  <p>
    Certificates are issued on the basis of attendance and assessment as
    applicable to the programme. A certificate confirms completion of the
    programme; it is not a professional licence or a guarantee of employment.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    All course material, exercises and documentation provided by PTCA remain our
    property. Learners may use them for personal study and may not reproduce,
    distribute or sell them without written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Educational content, not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Content published on this website, including articles in our resources
    section, is provided for education. It is not professional tax, legal or
    financial advice and does not create a professional relationship.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We take care to provide accurate information, but we do not warrant that the
    website is free of error or continuously available. To the extent permitted
    by law, PTCA is not liable for decisions you make in reliance on general
    information published here.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of Pakistan, and are subject to the
    jurisdiction of the courts of Karachi.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent to{' '}
    <a href={mailHref}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>